    description: "Repro: pyproject declares requests and beautifulsoup4, only requests installed -> requests imports stamped direct, bs4 stamped undeclared. Both stay tier 3. Fix options: unknown (not undeclared) when the dist->import map is incomplete, or a static dist->top-level-name table for common mismatches.\n\nFound by the 2026-10-10 docstring-staleness audit (reviewer + default-REJECT verifier, reproduced). Notebook: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_10102026.md."  # 7f7a
    fields:  # 7f7a
      statement: "An import of a declared dependency is never stamped 'undeclared'; a name py_deps cannot map stays unstamped."  # 7f7a
      root_cause: "py_deps maps dist names to import names via installed metadata; an uninstalled dist yields no mapping, and DependencyManifest.directness_for returns 'undeclared' for any unmatched module once a pyproject produced entries (supply_chain.py ~180-208)."  # 7f7a
